    "report": "The message notice now carries `listingId`, and the work is committed as `3f29b62` on `main`, not pushed. The full suite passes (269 suites, 1656 tests), and typecheck and lint are clean.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Messaging:** `MessageSentEvent` records the conversation's `listingId` at both places it is raised (when a conversation starts and when a message is added). `MessageSentHandler` passes it on.\n- **Shared kernel:** `MessageSentPayload` gains `listingId`, so the published contract includes it.\n- **Notifications:** `listingId` is read from the event, kept on the message notice and sent in the body. The existing `listing_id` column stores it, so no migration was needed.\n- **Tests:** the fixtures now include a listing id. Two end-to-end specs asserted the exact notice shape, so I updated them to expect `listingId`.\n\nWho is told, how often, delivery and retries, and the other notice kinds are untouched.\n\n**Decisions and unclear points**\n- **Committed on `main`.** You asked for the current branch and I followed that. The git guidance says to branch off the default branch first, so if you want a feature branch, it's a quick move.\n- **Legacy pending notices.** Message notices already stored but not yet accepted have no `listing_id`. They will be sent with `\"listingId\": null`. Notifications can't look up the listing without reading Messaging's data, so I didn't backfill. If the notification service can't handle null, those notices need a decision before deploy.\n- **Docs not updated.** ADR 57, `conventions/domain.yaml` and the storm YAML still describe the message event without `listingId`. I left them alone.\n- **Server not started.** No server was started, so port 4471 wasn't used.",
